# Nereids of Hesiod's Theogony, with the meaning of each name.
actaea    Nereid of the seashore
alimede   Nereid of the sea's counsel
autonoe   Nereid of her own mind
dynamene  Nereid of the power of the waves
eione     Nereid of the beach
eudora    Nereid of good gifts
eulimene  Nereid of the good harbour
galene    Nereid of the calm sea
halie     Nereid of the salt sea
laomedea  Nereid who rules the people
melite    Nereid, honey-sweet
menippe   Nereid of the strength of horses
nemertes  Nereid who never errs, wise like her father
panopea   Nereid who sees everything
pasithea  Nereid, goddess of all
polynoe   Nereid rich in reason
pronoe    Nereid of forethought
themisto  Nereid of divine law and custom
